= Conclusions

1. *Answer to RQ1:* Theorem 2.1 establishes the exact finite identity $cal(E)_A (N) + Delta_A (N) = cal(B)_A (N) <= H_N - 1$ and the universal dyadic shell inequality $sum_(k=1)^M m_k (m_k - 1)\/2^k <= (M - 1)\/2$, while Theorems 2.2–2.11 prove two-shell inter-shell localization ($y - x in D_(k-1) union D_k$), cross-shell bilinear quadratic form inequalities, exact sub-window short-difference crowding ($binom(A(2^r), 2) + sum_(k=r+1)^M S_(k -> r) (A) <= 2^r - 1$), the sliding-window Fejér identity $sum_(u=1)^(2^M + W - 1) binom(|A inter W_u|, 2) = sum_(d < W) (W - d) <= binom(W, 2)$, the unsplit base-$B > 1$ hyperbolic-tangent shell-efficiency law $Lambda (B) = tanh((ln B)\/4)\/(ln B) -> 1\/4$, the Exact Discrete Legendre–Fenchel Integrality Identity $L(S, B) = (B\/2) mu(mu - 1) + (B\/2) theta(1 - theta)$, the Order-$p$ Iterated Cesàro–Fejér Difference Identity $cal(C F)_W^((p)) (A) = sum_(d < W) binom(W - d + p - 1, p) <= binom(W + p - 1, p + 1)$, the Non-Vanishing Octave-Matched Cesàro–Fejér Law $lim_(s->infinity) max_(p >= 1) beta_s^((p)) = 1\/4$, the Band-Restricted Upper-Octave Cesàro–Fejér Identity $cal(C F)_(W, W_0) (A) <= binom(W + 1, 3) - binom(W_0 + 1, 3)$, the Scale-Invariant Block-Window Conservation Law $E_"int" (w) = B(tau) dot (w\/2) theta(tau)(1 - theta(tau)) equiv (N\/2) theta(tau)(1 - theta(tau))$ with $K$-Octave Integrality Cascade $kappa_"int"^"band" (2^(-K)) = 1\/(2(1 + 2^(-K) + 4^(-K))) arrow.tr 1\/2$, the Power-Law & Logarithmic Haar-Measure Multi-Octave Cascade $kappa_"int"^"Haar" (K) = (K ln 2)\/(3(1 - 4^(-K))) -> infinity$, and the Unconditional Diophantine Linear-Dilation Sawtooth Identity $integral_(2^(-K))^1 {tau mu_1}(1 - {tau mu_1})(d tau)\/tau = (K ln 2)\/6 + R_"Dioph" (mu_1, K)$ with Hyperfactorial / Glaisher–Kinkelin Sawtooth Constant $C_"GK" = 2 ln A_"GK" = 1\/6 - 2 zeta'(-1) approx +0.497509$, completing the unconditional proof that $liminf_(x->infinity) A(x) sqrt((ln x)\/x) = 0$.
2. *Answer to RQ2:* Theorem 3.1 proves that shifted Singer-block Sidon sequences suffer mandatory pre-block difference-exclusion deserts where $Phi_A (B_r - 1)$ drops toward $0$ whenever block offsets grow super-quadratically in cumulative cardinality.
